Title: Film Structure Demo
Draft date: 2026-01-02

# The Setup

[[
Act context
Function: Meeting the crew and getting a sense of the location on the Moon Base.
Dramatic Question: How will they handle the desolation and loneliness they face?
Shift: Alliances form and Jerry's left out to dry.
]]

## Welcome to the Moon Base

[[
Sequence context
Goal: Setting up the Moon Base Location and the characters living there.
]]

EXT.  MOON BASE - DAY

[[
Scene context
Goal: Show the setting of the story.
Outcome: We see that we are on a desolate moon base.
]]



INT. MOON BASE - DAY

[[
Scene context
Goal: Here we meet the three occupants of the Moon Base.
Conflict: We meet the small crew and try to work out what the situation is.
Outcome: We see that they are pretty bored.
]]



## What's wrong on the Moon Base?

[[
Sequence context
Goal: We've established the Moon Base, but what's the situation?
Conflict: Not much to do here.
Outcome: The crew is bored and a bit lonely.
]]

INT. MOON BASE  - DAY

[[
Scene context
Goal: Find out why they are so bored.
Conflict: The communication with Earth has been down for 5 days and they're getting behind on their favorite Soap Opera.
Outcome: They are constructing costumes to enact their own version of the story.
]]



## The Performance

[[
Sequence context
Goal: The three crew members need to perform a play for themselves in order to pass the time.
Conflict: It's hard and in the stress of the moment tempers flare as well as some unspoken passions.
Outcome: One of them is wounded.
]]

INT. MOON BASE - AUDITORIUM - NIGHT

[[
Scene context
Goal: Three crew mates must find a way to perform their interpretation of their favorite soap opera, two at a time for the third to watch,
Conflict: This is logistically difficult.
Outcome: They do a poor job of it.
]]



INT. MOON BASE - BACKSTAGE - NIGHT

[[
Scene context
Goal: Introduce the tension.
Conflict: Jerry didn't like Nancy's interpretation of the Soap Opera character "Debbie", he felt it lacked "gravitas"
Outcome: Nancy slapped the shit out of Jerry.
]]



INT. MOON BASE - INFIRMARY - NIGHT

[[
Scene context
Goal: Owen interrogates Jerry on what went down between him and Nancy.
Conflict: Owen is in love with Nancy and is very protective of her.
Outcome: Jerry trash talks Nancy and Owen slaps the shit out of Jerry (for a second time).
]]



# The Confrontation

[[
Act context
Function: Jerry has had enough of being slapped.
Dramatic Question: What will he do about it?
Shift: Jerry takes control of a situation that he was previously powerless in.
]]

## Jerry Fights Back

[[
Sequence context
Goal: Jerry is tired of being bullied and wants it to stop.
Conflict: Owen and Nancy react to Jerry for a reason, he's kind of a jerk.
Outcome: Jerry makes everything worse.
]]

INT. MOON BASE - CAFETERIA - MORNING

[[
Scene context
Goal: Jerry needs to air his grievances with Owen and Nancy.
Conflict: Jerry is tired of being the punching bag due to his spicy opinions.
Outcome: Owen and Nancy have had just about enough of Jerry's nonsense.
]]



INT. MOON BASE - COMMAND CHAMBER - DAY

[[
Scene context
Goal: Owen and Nancy need to deal with the issues with Jerry.
Conflict: Jerry is a jerk and is tired of being bullied.
Outcome: Jerry's approach at communication fails and Owen and Nancy decide to present a solution, to spend some time away from Jerry.
]]



## Intervention with Jerry

[[
Sequence context
Goal: Owen and Nancy need their space from Jerry and they want to let him know diplomatically.
Conflict: Jerry's not having it.
Outcome: Rather than a solution, things are even worse. Jerry feels like the victim, which he is, but he's also just so damn hard to deal with.
]]

INT. MOON BASE - KITCHEN - NIGHT

[[
Scene context
Goal: Jerry's misguided sense of justice allows him to feel that putting laxative in the Lasagna is a good way to resolve the conflict.
Conflict: Jerry's ideas are nearly always making things worse.
Outcome: Things get worse. Like, a lot worse.
]]



## The Lasagna

[[
Sequence context
Goal: Jerry puts laxative in the Lasagna, including his own.
Conflict: Laxative is a bad tool for conflict resolution.
Outcome: Every toilet is occupied by a pissed off individual.
]]

INT. MOON BASE - CAFETERIA - NIGHT

[[
Scene context
Goal: Jerry serves Laxative laced Lasagna to the crew, including himself.
Conflict: Laxatives make you poo
Outcome: Everyone is running for the toilets, not knowing why.
]]



# Act Three : Resolution

## The Confession

[[
Sequence context
Goal: Owen and Nancy want to know what happened, Jerry wants them to know he did it and why.
Conflict: Jerry thinks this will fix things.
Outcome: It doesn't.
]]

INT. MOON BASE - ARCADE - MORNING

[[
Scene context
Goal: Jerry invites Owen and Nancy to the arcade in the Moon Base to explain what he did.
Conflict: Jerry thinks this will help things, but Jerry is an idiot.
Outcome: Owen and Nancy are stunned by the idiocy of Jerry. The loud atmosphere helped nothing.
]]



INT. MOON BASE - COMMAND CHAMBER - DAY

[[
Scene context
Goal: Owen and Nancy decide they have had enough of Jerry. It's no longer tolerable, he needs to be dealt with.
Conflict: How to get rid of Jerry?
Outcome: They decide that the terms of their stay make it impossible to send him home, they will need to make a barrier and lock him in one part of the base until the contract is up and they go back to Earth.
]]



## The Quarantine

[[
Sequence context
Goal: Get Jerry to agree to terms of avoidance. That he stays away from Owen and Nancy.
Conflict: Jerry is difficult.
Outcome: Jerry reluctantly agrees. But it doesn't end well.
]]

INT. MOON BASE - CAFETERIA - NIGHT

[[
Scene context
Goal: Owen and Nancy break the news to Jerry.
Conflict: Jerry takes everything badly. How did he get this job in the first place? Aren't there psych evals for Moon Base operators?
Outcome: Jerry reluctantly agrees. But in a petty passive-aggressive move, he steals all the toilet paper and keeps it in his section of the base.
]]



INT. MOON BASE - MAIN AIRLOCK - DAWN

[[
Scene context
Goal: Owen and Nancy need to deal with Jerry once and for all.
Conflict: Jerry is resistant to any good solution.
Outcome: They ask Jerry to do some maintenance in the air lock, then they open the doors. Bye bye Jerry.
]]



# Loose Notes

[[
Location: Moon Base
Type: Int/Ext · Time Period: 2245 · Mood / Atmosphere: Desolate · Setting Description: It's a functional building in a desolate place. It's a little dated feeling even in the future.
]]
[[
Character: Owen Jenkins
Pronouns: he/him · Role: Protagonist · Occupation: Moon Base Commander · Age: Mid 30's · Character Summary: A mostly even tempered dude, in love with Nancy secretly.
]]
[[
Character: Nancy Flerkins
Pronouns: she/her · Role: Protagonist · Occupation: Moon Base Science Officer · Age: Mid 40's · Character Summary: A competent and strong person. Knows that Owen has feelings for her but doesn't reciprocate them.
]]
[[
Character: Jerry Perkins
Pronouns: he/him · Role: Antagonist · Occupation: Moon Base Maintenance · Age: Mid 30's · Character Summary: A truly irritating person. Can't read a room and always makes the wrong choice.
]]
